A||||2||FormulaJoe||Cooling System Question||||5||
Z||000000||FormulaJoe||06-28-2001||08:44 PM||||My Formula is taking longer to warm up than usual.  Noticed it this last weekend when I was driving around.  Whether was in the upper 70's low humidity and the car took about half an hour to reach "normal" operating temp.  What brought it to my attention was the idle, it was elevated (1200~1500 rpm) till the car finally warmed up.  After it warmed up fully the rpm dropped to normal (~1000rpm) but when I got out on the interstate to come home the temp started to drop again.  I am used to cars overheating on me and  looking for the cause, but this is a kind of new one on me.  Only thing I can think of is the thermostat went.  But usually when a thermostat goes it over heats not over cools.  Any ideas guys?||||reg||5
Z||000001||acehilton||06-28-2001||08:57 PM||||Sounds like a thermostat to me.  I have had them fail both ways, it's just a little less exciting when they stick open!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||06-28-2001||08:58 PM||||If the thermostat is stuck open it takes forever to warm up. Just open the cap and pull the thermostat out. If it's open or not seated right that's the problem.||||reg||1
